@bs-humany/skeleton

This package is in the Data tier of ADR-009 and is distributed under Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (see LICENSE). Its landmarks, local frames, joint centres,
rest transforms, collision proxies and the profiles traced from the bone meshes are derived from
the meshes in @bs-humany/assets-anatomical, and so from the following:

  "BodyParts3D - The Database Center for Life Science - CC-BY-SA 2.1 Japan"
  "Z-Anatomy - The libre 3D atlas of anatomy - CC-BY-SA 4.0"

Z-Anatomy authors: Kousaku Okubo (original BodyParts3D model), Gauthier Kervyn (design, 3D,
anatomy), Marcin Zielinski (Blender add-on), Lluis Vinent (Unity development).
Source: https://github.com/LluisV/Z-Anatomy (Resources/Models/FBX/SkeletalSystem100.fbx) and
https://github.com/Z-Anatomy/Models-of-human-anatomy.

src/muscleViaPoints.ts also carries the muscle via points of MyoSuite myo_sim (MyoHub,
Apache-2.0), moved into this skeleton's bone frames by `pnpm generate:via-points`. Apache-2.0
permits their use in a CC BY-SA work; the licence and the pinned commit are in
tools/validate-external/myo_sim, and the root NOTICE says what else is taken from that model.

The data and the code that holds it share the same source files here, so the package as a whole
carries the data's licence. The other bs-humany code packages, which load this data, remain
Apache-2.0: they are not derivatives of it. See ADR-009 and ADR-011, and the root NOTICE.
